On August 26, the police had recovered the body of Zahid Iqbal, a resident of Padshahi Bagh in Jhelum Darya.
His family members had accused his friends of killing him as his mobile and other belongings were missing.
In the report, the police said that the phone and SIM of the deceased were checked and it was found that her phone was being used by a woman in Soura.
During interrogation, the woman said she was given this phone by one of her relatives Ruhail Gauahar.
Ruhail also resides in Padashahi Bagh and he was a friend of late Zahid.
On August 25, Ruhail went to Jhelum with Zahid after Namaaz-e-Jumma.
Zahid opened his clothes and kept all the stuff on the shore, while Ruhail went to the other way to smoke cigarettes.
When he came back, Zahid was not there, he had only clothes.
Ruhail searched Zahid, but he was not found.
On this, he picked up his mobile phone, watch and other belongings and kept it for his use.
He did not tell anyone that Zahid had drowned.
According to the police, Zahid died due to drowning and it has also been confirmed in the post-mortem.
However, Ruhail has been taken into custody under Section 404 of the IPC for concealing facts and the belongings of the deceased.
