NSA accuses "internal error" instead of hackers for website to crash
The mystical national security agency said on Friday that our website was closed for a few hours due to some technical shortages, not because of hackers as some people claimed online.
"NSA.gov was not in access for several hours tonight, which was caused by an internal error during the pre-determined update," the intelligence agency said in an e-mailed statement.
This problem will be resolved tonight.
This claim is not true that this obstruction, the delivery denial of service [D.D.O.S.] was caused by the attack.
