New research has shown that we work with complete sincerity and dedication in the morning.
Don't lie to anyone and don't think like stealing or cheating.
But in the evening, our mind changes and we start moving against the rule by keeping the ideal aside.
Researchers have given many interesting facts in this research from Harvard University and the David Aclues School of Business of Utâauto.
According to the researchers, we prefer moral values by not having the stress of work in the morning, but honesty decreases due to fatigue or excessive pressure in the evening.
For this, the researchers conducted two experiments.
He asked some people to tell the number of points on the computer screen.
For example, people had to tell whether the point is higher on the left or on the right.
The participants were told that if they give wrong answers instead of the right answer, they will be given money.
In this experiment, it was seen that the people who were used between 8 and 12 in the morning did not make any mistake and gave the correct answer.
At the same time, between 12 noon and 6 p.m., while experimenting on people, it was found that he deliberately gave wrong answers by putting his principles on hold.
Due to this, the researchers managed to prove that the greed for money in the morning does not make any difference to our honesty, but in the evening, we stayphysicism to give importance to morality.
This research has been published in the latest issue of psychological science.
