The Special Task Force (STF) has unearthed the fraud in the PMT of the year 2012.
The STF has found irregularities in the roll numbers of 700 students.
Out of these, about 125 students had taken admission in medical colleges.
Now the admission of these students can be cancelled.
The Medical Education Department has started brainstorming to cancel the admissions of these students after the STF's revelation.
According to the information, the department is waiting to meet the list of all these suspicious students from the STF.
The list will be sent to Vyapam to cancel the eligibility of the students involved.
However, in this case, the department is also seeking legal advice.
According to departmental officials, it has been a year for the students who took admission in the year 2012, so it is necessary to seek legal advice in this matter.
The medical education department officials are not in a position to say anything as the case is still confined to the STF investigation.
Vyapam director Tarun Pithore said if the STF submits a list of suspected students along with evidence, their admissions will be cancelled immediately.
On the other hand, Director Medical Education Dr Nirbhay Srivastava said that it has not even refused to cancel the admissions of the students if they are found to be correct.
According to STF officials, fake students involved in the 2012 PMT are being investigated.
After the investigation, the list of suspicious students will be submitted to Vyapam.
Vyapam had cancelled the eligibility of 345 suspected students appeared in the PMT examination held in the year 2013.
Out of these 345, the medical education department has revoked the admission of 84 so far.
Ijaz Jaan, MLA from Poonch assembly constituency, inaugurated a water cooler at the gurdwara complex.
The MLA said that a large number of people come and go to the gurdwara, but due to the lack of proper arrangement of drinking water, a water cooler has been installed here.
This will provide cold water to the people.
Pure plain water will be available during the winter season.
This will solve the problem of drinking water for the devotees.
Members of the Gurdwara Committee and others were also present on the occasion.
After the general elections, if the new government continues the policy to stop selling kerosene through ration, then kerosene will not be available at these shops in half a dozen states.
Punjab, Haryana, Punjab, Rajasthan and Uttarakhand are among the states where kerosene will be discontinued.
Kerosene is also set to be discontinued in Karnataka, Tamil Nadu and some northeastern states.
According to sources in the petroleum ministry, a decision will be taken to stop the sale of kerosene at PDS shops in the states on two basis.
First of all, electricity connections are being built rapidly in rural areas.
The second base is the LPG connection.
That is, the sale of PDS kerosene is being discontinued in most of the rural families of the states where LPG connections have been given.
The Ministry of Petroleum has made preparations in this regard.
Since October 2013, PDS kerosene has already come to a standstill.
According to sources, Punjab, Haryana, Maharashtra and Uttarakhand have significantly reduced the kerosene quota under this policy.
Punjab's quota was reduced from 2.72 lakh kils to one lakh kils.
In Uttarakhand, 70 per cerosene quota has been reduced by about 40 per cent.
Despite this reduction, there has been no reports of kerosene shortage from these states.
The Ministry is assuming that it is clear that kerosene has been used for adulteration.
At present, there is a difference of Rs 37 in the price of PDS kerosene and diesel.
This encourages adulterators.
Oil companies will sell kerosene at a full price in states where PDS will be discontinued.
At present, oil companies are facing a loss of more than Rs 39 per litre on kerosene.
The burden of kerosene subsidy is estimated to be about Rs 31 thousand crore in the year 2013-14.
The accused used to forgery in the name of horse-trading by opening the accounts of the investors citing the trading firm.
For the first time in the state, there has been talk of cheating of crores of rupees.
The police have not been able to reach the spot yet, but the police have detained seven people, including the accused who saw his work in the state.
This gang used to operate a fake commodity market in the name of MetaTrader-5.
The company's players used to take cash money from the investors and create a fake ID on a fogus software.
Due to this, the stocks purchased by the investors were visible to the accused.
It used to know at what price which share was bought.
In fact, no shares were purchased and there was no transaction for it, because no demat account of investors was opened and shares were shown to be false on this fake software.
The police are suspecting that hundreds of people have been involved in this gang.
Two to five lakh rupees were invested in the name of giving profit from each investor.
Amit Soni, the main accused, has been detained by the cyber cell from Jodhpur, while his six other accomplices have been arrested from Indore.
According to ADG Cyber Cell Ashok Dohre, any stock trading company is required to join the stock exchange as a trading firm.
After this, the company can get stock trading done to the investors through it.
Then the investor's demat account is opened, so that shares can be bought and sold for him, but this company named MetaTrader 5 was neither associated with any exchange nor used to conduct stock trading.
This company had bought a server for itself on September 24, 2012, citing trading in the name of WinTrade.
Since then, people have been cheated in the name of investment through this company.
At present, eight traders from Indore have come to the fore who complained to the cyber cell.
Even after selling his purchased shares for profit, his money was not transferred to the account.
On this, he started asking for the profit amount from the doers of the company.
Investors are even saying that on the fake ID given to them, the price of their purchased shares was always shown to be less.
This price used to be decided by the accused at their own level.
The company has appointed its CEOs and agents in Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh and Maharashtra.
The agents used to advise people to join this company by luring them with more profits.
After this, two lakh rupees were deposited from someone and five lakh rupees were deposited.
The players of this team keep setting new records every day in Tests and now their status is gradually increasing even in ODIs.
There was also an excellent example of this on Thursday when a good New Zealand team was defeated by Bangladesh to take an unstoppable lean in the ODI series.
Sohag Ghazi and Mashrafe Murtaza helped Bangladesh take an unassailable 2-0 lead in the three-match series by defeating New Zealand by 40 runs in the second ODI.
This is Bangladesh's sixth consecutive victory in ODIs against New Zealand.
Earlier, New Zealand had lost the series 0-4 in the 2010 tour of Bangladesh.
Chasing a target of 248 from Bangladesh, New Zealand lost wickets at regular intervals in front of Ghazi (34/3) spin and Murtaza (43/3).
For New Zealand, Ross Taylor were the top scorers with 45, while Corey Anderson scored 37.
Kyle Mills did an nought, while Nathan McCullum contributed 25, but none of the team's batsmen were able to convert a good start into a big innings, which led the team to a defeat.
Earlier, Bangladesh were bowled for 247 in 49 overs despite a half-centurie from Tamim Iqbal (58).
James Neesham and Anderson took eight wickets.
Anderson took four wickets for 40, while Neesham took four wickets for 53 runs.
Tameem has become the highest run-scorer in Bangladesh.
Tamim, who has surpassed Shakib Al Hasaan, has scored 3702 runs in 124 matches.
The third and final match of the series will be played in Fatullah on Sunday.
