Punjab State Power Corporation (PWC) has earned crores of rupees every day.
In such a situation, all the employees are forced to work in fear of accidents.
There is an atmosphere of panic among the staff working due to the collapse of cement from the roofs of this building.
This building, which was built in 1913, had the office of the Municipal Corporation.
The building was handed over to the electricity board in the year 1975.
In the name of repair, the department is shruggling only by getting the color groan.
The condition of the building has deteriorated so much that the employees are also afraid to sit in it.
The condition of the building is so crumbling that often the plaster falls from the ceilings.
In the last one month, cement has fallen from the roofs of four rooms.
A woman employee was also injured in the incident.
JE and revenue accountants escaped unhurt in the incident.
At present, about four and a half hundred employees work in the building.
This includes 5 XENs, 12 SDOs, 20 Junior Engineers, 150 Clerk Staff, 200 technical staff and 20 other staff members.
Recently, nothing has been done by Powercom high officials about their safety so far.
Three rooms, scooters and bicycle stands, two rooms in the upper floor have completely collapsed.
In such a situation, the condition of the building can be easily estimated.
