Former military ruler General Pervez Musharraf's bail plea to assassinate Lal Masjid cleric has been adjourned till November 4th.
The next hearing of the case against Musharraf will take place on November 11.
Maulvi Ghazi Abdul Rasheeed was killed in a military operation carried out against radicals hiding in the Lal Masjid in 2007.
In this case, the police have already given a big relief by making Musharraf innocent.
According to the police, Musharraf did not have a direct hand in the cleric's murder.
Additional District and Sessions Judge (ADSJ) Wajid Ali Musharraf is hearing the bail plea of Islamabad-based Additional District and Sessions Judge (ADSJ).
During the hearing, Tariq Assad, a representative of the Lal Masjid Shuhada Foundation and the complainant's lawyer, alleged that the police have destroyed all the evidence to prove Musharraf innocent.
The lawyer sought some time from the court to produce more evidence in this case.
After this, the court deferred the hearing on Musharraf's bail plea till November 4th.
A meeting was held in the town on Thursday regarding the welfare of the disabled.
The meeting was presided over by senior vice-president Vinod Sharma.
