The two agencies stole data passing through the huge fiber optic cable network laid by Yahoo and Google.
The Washington Post quoted a top secret document dated January 9, 2013, saying that more than 18 crore documents were collected in just 3 days after the programme was launched.
These include email, text, audio and video messages.
According to the Washington Post, the program was run out of the United States and an benami telecommunications provider helped the NSA to have access to this information.
According to the newspaper, it was easier for the NSA to run this program outside the U.S. because such campaigns in the U.
NSA Chief General Keith Alexander, during a press conference in Washington, denied these allegations and said, As far as I know, it has never happened.
