Some people are born with a silver spoon, some with their hard work makes life ideal and people take inspiration from them.
One such name also comes from Late Dhirubhai Ambani.
Dhirubhai Ambani, the third son of Hirachand Gowardhandas Ambani, was born on December 28, 1932.
Dhirubhai was the third of five siblings.
Five children of the family include Ramnikalal, Natwar Lal, Dhirubhai and two sisters Trilochana and Jasumati.
Dhirubhai had to give up his studies only after high school due to financial constraints.
Dhirubhai had started helping the house financially in childhood.
At this time he used to set up a bhajiye shop near Girnar, the income of the shop was limited on the number of tourists coming here.
Talking about Dhirubhai's first job, in 1949, at the age of 17, he reached the city of Aiden in Yemen with a ship named Kabota.
His elder brother Ramniklal had made all the arrangements for him, so he did not have any problem in getting a job abroad.
But there was something else going on in Dhirubhai's mind.
That is why in 1954 he came back.
In 1955, he reached Mumbai to try his luck by keeping Rs 500 in his pocket.
That's where his business journey began.
Dhirubhai Ambani took such steps from here that he has never looked back.
His name became famous not only in the country but also abroad.
Dhirubhai Ambani left the world on July 6, 20202.
He was currently the owner of Rs 62000 crore.
At present, his sons Mukesh Ambani and Anil Ambani are taking care of their Sultanate.
Like the father, today the name of these two brothers is also one of the businessmen of the international level.
Who doesn't know the Ambani family today?
Dhirubhai, Kokilaben, two sons Mukesh and Anil Ambani and their wives Nita Ambani and Tina Ambani.
