There has been a new politics to change boards in municipalities.
Recently, the Trinamool turned into a board due to the defection of councillors of the Congress-ledency in Sanithia municipality of Veerbhum district.
This change took place due to most Congress councillors, including the chairman of the municipality, joining the Trinamool.
Not only the Congress, but some councillors of the CPI(M), the CPI(M) and the Forward Block have suppressed the TMC here.
Trinamool Congress general secretary Mukul Roy considers this a good sign for the party.
He said 10 Congress councillors, including Sanithia municipality chairman Virendra Parikh and Congress leader Viplav Dutta, joined the TMC.
Some of the Left Front councillors, including the CPI(M), have also joined the TMC flag.
Everyone has written to the District Magistrate under the Bengal Municipal Act that they have become a part of the Trinamool and according to the number force, the Sanithia municipal board has also come under the control of the TMC.
Rai also claims that everyone agrees with the roadmap of development in Bengal led by Chief Minister Mamata Banerjee.
Leaders of other parties, including the Congress, the CPI(M), the CPI(M), and Forward Block, are moving to join the Trinamool Congress.
Eligible leaders of any party are welcome to the Trinamool.
Ahead of the November 22 municipal elections, due to the defection of Congress councillors in Saithia municipality, the Trinamool's take-noction of the municipal board is considered important in political circles.
Earlier, there is an example of the Trinamool's taking over the Congress-ruled municipal board in Haldia and Nadia.
When the Trinamool takes control of the municipal board in the districts due to defection, those who join the party get a grand welcome at the Trinamool Bhavan in Kolkata.
Trinamool Congress general secretary Mukul Roy is excited to break away from other parties and joining the TMC.
He said that those who broke away from any party are welcome to the TMC.
She claims that the faith of the people under the leadership of Chief Minister Mamata Banerjee is increasing, as a result of which people want to join the Trinamool.
However, the CPI(M), the main opposition party, says leaders of other parties are being intimidated and intimidated.
People are joining the Trinamool Congress, fearing the terror of the Trinamool Congress.
The CPI(M) considers the change in the boards of elected local bodies as an impact on democracy.
In a democratic manner, any party has the right to increase its mass base, but it is necessary to question the rationale for a change of opinion in power.
Australian woman appeals against Thai imprisonment period
