Businesswoman Nita Ambani, the wife of India's wealthiest businessman, is celebrating her 50th birthday on Friday.
Arrangements have been made to make the birthday special.
The city of Jodhpur has been selected for the royal party.
About 11 km from Umaid Bhawan, the famous Balsamand Lake has been decorated as a venue.
On Friday, all the guests will gather here for Lakshmi Puja on her birthday.
After this, a dance program has also been organized.
It has been choreographed by famous Bollywood celebrity Vaibhavi Merchet.
Nita Ambani and her daughter Isha are also expected.
Neeta and Isha are both professional classical dancers.
250 VVIPs have also been invited for this royal party.
These include Raja Gagsinh II, the owner of the Jodhpur royal family and Ummaid Bhavan and his family, Tata, Birla, Mittal, Godrej, among others.
L.N. Mittal, Sachin Tendulkar, film actors Anil Kapoor, Aamir Khan, A.R. Rehman arrived in Jodhpur on Thursday evening.
32 chartered aircraft have been arranged to ferry guests.
